sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If two rational straight lines commensurable in square only are added together, then the whole is irrational; let it be called <i>binomial.</i>
----
proof:

Let two rational straight lines {AB} and {BC} commensurable in square only be added together.

I say that the whole {AC} is irrational.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="230" height="80" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.36 diagram" src="propX36.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Joyce's figure: the line AC with B on it (X0, X1 are off-canvas
    // anchors for the line sliders). Added, hidden at rest: transparent
    // targets AB, BC (;0;0;0) so the two parts can light separately.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): X0, X1 (free, off-canvas)
    // and A, B, C (line sliders), all givens; nothing is deferred.
    var ALL = ["A","B","C","AB","BC","AC"];
